# Phase 3.1 Dedup Agent: comparison/normalization deps. jellyfish + rapidfuzz
# (string similarity) and usaddress (address parsing) cover the live
# propose_merge / dedup_status MCP tools. pandas is the DataFrame interchange
# format the batch DedupAgent (agents/dedup/agent.py, splink_runner.py) builds
# candidate pairs in; it is light enough for the worker image (no torch) and is
# imported lazily, so the API process never loads it. These import cleanly in
# the deployed image.
jellyfish~=1.1
rapidfuzz~=3.10
usaddress~=0.5
pandas~=2.2

# Phase 3.1 Dedup Agent: OPTIONAL probabilistic-linkage accelerator, EXCLUDED.
# splink + duckdb give EM-trained weights, but splink_runner wraps the import
# in try/except and falls back to the pure-Python comparison scoring when they
# are absent, so the agent is fully functional without them. sentence-
# transformers pulls torch (multi-GB) and is declared-but-unused (the embedding
# comparisons take precomputed vectors), so it stays out too. Re-enable splink/
# duckdb in a dedicated heavier batch-worker image when EM-calibrated scoring is
# wanted; keep them out of the API/worker image to stay within the 1G limit.
# splink~=4.0
# duckdb~=1.1
# sentence-transformers~=3.2
# pyarrow~=18.0

